"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does GPU docking at 54000 rotations improve rank1 or best50 DockQ over 3600 rotations within identical complete-workflow budgets?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Denser angular coverage improves best50 recovery more consistently than rank1 because scoring can still favor wrong poses.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"At 54000 versus 3600 rotations, best50 DockQ rises over 0.01 beyond noise on all 4 cases; rank1 changes remain separate.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"At 54000 versus 3600 rotations, at least 1 case lacks best50 DockQ gain over 0.01 beyond noise, or dense search misses budget.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Build frozen docking, reconstruction, evaluation and billing harness. Compare CPU and GPU at 3600 rotations; require agreement, then compare GPU 54000 versus 3600 using 50 poses, 7 timing blocks, per-case rank1/best50 and common complete-workflow budgets.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Published MEGADOCK GPU study measured docking acceleration at default 3600 rotations; it did not compare dense-search rank1 and best50 DockQ. [prior]\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"prior\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/1752-0509-9-S1-S6\",\"quote\":\"MEGADOCK uses an n_{ θ } value of 3,600 as the default setting.\"}],\"value\":3600}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Does 54000-rotation GPU search improve retained-pose recovery or first-ranked accuracy within complete-workflow budgets on these 4 unbound cases?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Independent transform reconstruction and DockQ fixtures validate execution; CPU outputs anchor identical GPU settings before dense quality evaluation.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"dockq\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wallnerlab/DockQ/master/README.md\",\"quote\":\"By default, DockQ will try to find the optimal mapping between interfaces found in the native and in the model.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Exposed 4-case replication only; no biological efficacy, unseen holdout, broad accuracy scaling, or CPU-only market-cost claim. Scientific acceptance remains gated.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:prior\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/1752-0509-9-S1-S6\",\"quote\":\"MEGADOCK uses an n_{ θ } value of 3,600 as the default setting.\",\"supports\":\"Standard angular setting in nearest retrieved open published GPU performance comparison; mathematical symbol transcribed as extracted.\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:dockq\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wallnerlab/DockQ/master/README.md\",\"quote\":\"By default, DockQ will try to find the optimal mapping between interfaces found in the native and in the model.\",\"supports\":\"Pin mapping policy; same documentation supplies model/native command and explicit mapping option.\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:standard_rotations\",\"name\":\"Standard angular search\",\"value\":3600,\"unit\":\"rotations\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"3600 angles\",\"page_setting\":\"Default standard rotation sampling.\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akiyamalab/MEGADOCK/master/doc/README.md\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:dense_rotations\",\"name\":\"Documented -D angular search\",\"value\":54000,\"unit\":\"rotations\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"54000 angles\",\"page_setting\":\"Dense -D rotation sampling.\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akiyamalab/MEGADOCK/master/doc/README.md\"}
